                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_06\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit (fix_commit_diff.txt) modifies JavaSource/org/unitime/timetable/onlinesectioning/model/XReservation.java, changing the `Group`, `Curriculum`, and `Course` cases of a switch statement so that each uses its own type-specific ApplicationProperty settings (ReservationPriorityGroup/Curriculum/Course, ReservationCanOverLimitGroup/Curriculum/Course, ReservationMustBeUsedGroup/Curriculum/Course, ReservationAllowOverlapGroup/Curriculum/Course) instead of incorrectly reusing the Individual-suffixed properties. This matches the fix commit message: \"fixed an issue taking all the properties (reservation priority, must be used, can assign over limit, allow overlap) from individual reservation\".\n\ncandidate_06 introduces this exact switch statement for the first time. It adds the new ApplicationProperty enum constants (ReservationPriorityIndividual, ReservationPriorityGroup, ReservationPriorityCurriculum, ReservationPriorityCourse, ReservationPriorityOverride, ReservationPriorityDummy, and corresponding MustBeUsed/CanOverLimit/AllowOverlap variants) in ApplicationProperty.java, and simultaneously adds the buggy switch block in XReservation.java's constructor where the `Group`, `Curriculum`, and `Course` cases all copy-paste the `...Individual` property calls instead of their own type-specific ones (only `Individual` and `Override`/`Dummy` cases used the correct properties). Interestingly, in the same commit, StudentSectioningDatabaseLoader.java correctly uses the type-specific properties (e.g., ReservationPriorityGroup for group reservations), showing the copy-paste error was isolated to the XReservation.java switch statement.\n\nNo earlier candidate contains this switch statement or these ApplicationProperty enum values at all (they are newly introduced), so the bug could not have existed before candidate_06. All later candidates that touch this code (candidate_08) merely inherit the pre-existing bug without altering these specific lines. Therefore candidate_06 is the commit that introduced the bug.\n"
